.TH SDL_BYTEORDER 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_BYTEORDER \- A macro that reports the target system\(aqs byte order.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_endian.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_BYTEORDER   SDL_LIL_ENDIAN___or_maybe___SDL_BIG_ENDIAN
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is set to either
.BR SDL_LIL_ENDIAN
or
.BR SDL_BIG_ENDIAN
(and maybe other values in the future, if something else becomes popular)\[char46] This can be tested with the preprocessor, so decisions can be made at compile time\[char46]

.IP
.EX
#if SDL_BYTEORDER == SDL_BIG_ENDIAN
SDL_Log("This system is bigendian.");
#endif
.EE
.PP

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_LIL_ENDIAN (3),
.BR SDL_BIG_ENDIAN (3)
